1) Building:

        Lapack/Blas:

                sudo apt-get install libblas-dev liblapack-dev

        GMP:

                sudo apt-get install libgmp3-dev   

2) Make sure your .cabal test-suite stanza declares it as a build tool dependency: 

        test-suite my-tests
          type:                exitcode-stdio-1.0
          hs-source-dirs:      test
          main-is:             Spec.hs
          build-depends:       base, hspec, your-package-name
          build-tool-depends:  hspec-discover:hspec-discover   

3) Run cabal update so the solver can find and build hspec-discover:

        cabal update

4) Rebuild:

        cabal build all

        Cabal will now build hspec-discover as a dependency and place it on the PATH 
        for the test-suite build. 

        The key piece is build-tool-depends — without it, Cabal v2 doesn't know 
        it needs to make the binary available to GHC.

5) ghci:
        
        5.1) Disable wrong ghci warning about missing modules when loading a .hs file:
                
                (That's the key detail. The warning is a known false positive in the REPL context (tracked as Cabal issue #4711))

                :set -Wno-missing-home-modules   

        5.2) cd into the same directory where stearnswharf.cabal resides

        5.3) cabal ghci

        5.4) :l src/StearnsWharf.Beam

        

